<section class="faqs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">Common questions</div>
    <h2>Things parents ask first.</h2>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Is the clinic only for kids trying out for the Peaches?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>Nope. It's open to anyone — Peaches families, non-Peaches families, kids trying out for any travel organization, kids just sharpening up for next season. The work is the work. If she plays softball, she'll get something out of it.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What if my daughter is more advanced (or less) than the others?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>Good coaches teach to the player in front of them, not the average. Our college players are used to running stations where every kid is at a different point — they'll meet her where she is. The drills scale up or down naturally, and the work is the same whether she's in her first travel season or her fifth.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Will the coaches at this clinic be evaluating for tryouts?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>No. A few Peaches coaches will be on site to support, but they aren't running evaluations and they aren't taking notes. Every player wears the same unnumbered clinic t-shirt — no numbers, no rankings, no rosters going into July. She can take risks, mess up, ask questions, and try things that don't quite work without any of it counting against her at tryouts.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>What if it rains?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>Light rain, we play through it — softball doesn't stop for sprinkles. Heavy weather, we'll reschedule.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Refund policy?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>No refunds. Registration covers coaches, field time, and your daughter's t-shirt — all of which are locked in once she signs up. If something comes up, reach out and we'll do our best to credit you toward a future Peaches clinic, but we can't refund the registration.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Does this guarantee her a spot at tryouts or on the team?<span class="icon">+</span></summary>
      <div class="faq-body">
        <p>It does not. Tryouts are tryouts. What this clinic does is make sure she's not seeing the format, the speed, or the nerves for the first time on tryout day. That's a real edge — but it's not a guarantee, and we'd never sell it as one.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

